WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.600
Elena's employer provides group life insurance.

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:08.680
The employer or eligible trustees hold the master policy, while

3
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:10.680
Elena is an insured employee.

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:16.180
She receives a certificate describing her protection, who receives benefits

5
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:21.240
and important rights. Under Maryland's employer-group rule, this

6
00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.740
coverage benefits people other than the employer.

7
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.600
It is different from a business buying key-person coverage for its

8
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.740
own loss. Eligible employees may include all employees or qualifying

9
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:38.040
classes. Read the policy's eligibility terms rather than assuming that

10
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:42.440
every worker, contractor or family member is automatically covered.

11
00:00:43.026 --> 00:00:48.146
Group premiums may come from the employer, employees or both.

12
00:00:49.086 --> 00:00:53.026
When employees contribute, the plan is contributory.

13
00:00:53.746 --> 00:00:56.606
When they do not, it is noncontributory.

14
00:00:57.246 --> 00:01:02.246
Maryland's employer-group rule generally requires coverage of all eligible

15
00:01:02.246 --> 00:01:07.366
employees in a noncontributory plan, except written rejections

16
00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:10.086
and the stated insurability exception.

17
00:01:10.786 --> 00:01:15.846
Covered arrangements may extend protection to a spouse, domestic partner

18
00:01:16.386 --> 00:01:21.226
or dependent children. The amount on a dependent cannot exceed the

19
00:01:21.226 --> 00:01:23.886
employee's amount under the rule taught here.

20
00:01:24.306 --> 00:01:27.906
A dependent's coverage and conversion rights require their own attention.

21
00:01:28.932 --> 00:01:32.172
Marcus leaves his job and loses the covered group life insurance.

22
00:01:33.292 --> 00:01:38.012
Maryland's conversion rule lets an eligible insured obtain individual life

23
00:01:38.012 --> 00:01:42.312
coverage from the insurer without new evidence of insurability.

24
00:01:43.172 --> 00:01:48.172
The ordinary application and first-premium deadline is thirty-one days after

25
00:01:48.172 --> 00:01:52.052
termination of employment or eligible membership.

26
00:01:52.932 --> 00:01:58.392
The available form is a form the insurer customarily issues, other

27
00:01:58.392 --> 00:02:02.292
than term insurance, subject to the stated conditions.

28
00:02:03.292 --> 00:02:07.932
Conversion preserves an opportunity for coverage,

29
00:02:08.512 --> 00:02:10.692
not the old group price.

30
00:02:11.572 --> 00:02:16.192
The premium reflects the permitted form, amount, risk class and attained

31
00:02:16.192 --> 00:02:21.666
age. Suppose Marcus loses eighty thousand dollars of

32
00:02:21.666 --> 00:02:26.026
group coverage but becomes eligible for thirty thousand dollars under another

33
00:02:26.026 --> 00:02:29.006
group policy within the stated thirty-one-day period.

34
00:02:29.826 --> 00:02:34.699
Under the Maryland conversion amount rule, the maximum is fifty thousand

35
00:02:34.699 --> 00:02:40.146
dollars. The statute also requires written notice of conversion rights and

36
00:02:40.146 --> 00:02:44.746
provides an extension when that notice is missing or late, within

37
00:02:44.746 --> 00:02:49.166
its outer limit. If an insured dies while entitled to convert

38
00:02:49.166 --> 00:02:53.946
but before the individual policy is effective, the amount available for

39
00:02:53.946 --> 00:02:57.926
conversion is payable under the group policy, even without the application

40
00:02:57.926 --> 00:03:00.964
or first premium. Now change the facts.

41
00:03:01.804 --> 00:03:06.024
The employer's entire group policy ends, or a covered class is

42
00:03:06.024 --> 00:03:10.084
removed, instead of Marcus simply leaving his job.

43
00:03:10.724 --> 00:03:13.524
A separate Maryland provision addresses this event.

44
00:03:14.344 --> 00:03:17.004
It protects an insured who has been covered for at least

45
00:03:17.004 --> 00:03:21.424
five years before termination, subject to the conversion conditions.

46
00:03:22.124 --> 00:03:25.524
The policy may limit the individual amount to the lesser of

47
00:03:25.524 --> 00:03:29.717
the lost coverage after the specified new-group offset, or ten thousand

48
00:03:29.717 --> 00:03:35.284
dollars. Do not apply this five-year requirement and possible cap to

49
00:03:35.284 --> 00:03:39.144
every ordinary employment-termination conversion question.

50
00:03:40.194 --> 00:03:45.554
Maryland permits an insured to assign group-life rights and benefits

51
00:03:45.554 --> 00:03:50.714
under an arrangement among the insured, policyholder and insurer.

52
00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:56.414
The assigned rights can include conversion and naming a beneficiary.

53
00:03:57.494 --> 00:04:01.114
The assignee receives the rights actually assigned.

54
00:04:02.254 --> 00:04:07.214
Follow the arrangement and the insurer's notice process; do not assume

55
00:04:07.214 --> 00:04:09.954
that every assignment transfers every right.

56
00:04:10.774 --> 00:04:15.194
Elena should understand what she controls after an assignment and who

57
00:04:15.194 --> 00:04:17.334
can exercise the transferred rights.

58
00:04:18.494 --> 00:04:23.334
For an exam scenario, identify the event first, then the right,

59
00:04:24.094 --> 00:04:27.794
the responsible person, the amount and the deadline.
